  "problem": "In a medical study, the concentration of a drug in a patient\u2019s bloodstream (in $mg/L$) after $t$ hours is given by the function $C(t).$ The values of $C(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| **$t$** | $2.0$ | $2.4$ | $2.8$ | $3.2$ | $3.6$ | $4.0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$C(t)$** | $12.4$ | $11.8$ | $11.0$ | $10.4$ | $9.8$ | $9.2$ |\n\nApproximate the drug\u2019s concentration instantaneous rate of change at $t=3.2$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=0.4.$\n\nThe drug\u2019s concentration at $t=3.2$ is decreasing at approximately \n{{field-1}} $mg/L$ per hour.",
